# store/data/ used to be ignored here, with the reason "derived view rebuilt
# from the v2 sources (data/import_v2.py) — never commit; the v2 files in
# wc2026/ remain the authority until cutover". That premise expired on
# 2026-07-24, when era v1-epl-2026-27 began writing PRIMARY records into the
# same files — locks, results, odds snapshots, evidence bundles that exist
# nowhere else on disk. From then until 2026-08-26 the live competition's
# only copy of its own data was untracked and unbacked-up.
#
# Tracked from 2026-08-26. The v2-wc2026 era rows in these files are still a
# rebuildable derived view, and audit/selftest.py's bit-identical recompute
# gate is what proves it — so committing them costs a few hundred KB and
# losing them would cost the live window everything.
__pycache__/
